# {{FEATURE_NAME}} — Task List

> **Plan reference:** `{{FEATURE_ID}}-plan` (must have `status: approved` before tasks begin)  
> **Convention:** Mark tasks `[/]` when in progress, `[x]` when complete. Update `updated_at` on every save.

---

## Phase 1: Preparation & Domain Modeling

- [ ] Define and document all data interfaces and contracts (no implementation code yet)
- [ ] Create database migration files (if applicable)
- [ ] Set up any required environment variables or configuration entries
- [ ] Verify all dependencies and libraries are available

## Phase 2: TDD — Red Phase (Write Failing Tests First)

> **Rule:** Do NOT write any production code in this phase. Tests must fail first.

- [ ] Write unit test for [domain entity or use case] — expect failure
- [ ] Write unit test for [second domain entity or use case] — expect failure
- [ ] Write integration test for [API endpoint or service boundary] — expect failure

## Phase 3: TDD — Green Phase (Minimum Implementation to Pass Tests)

> **Rule:** Write only the minimum code needed to make each test pass. No gold-plating.

- [ ] Implement [domain entity or use case] — make unit test pass
- [ ] Implement [second domain entity or use case] — make unit test pass
- [ ] Implement [API endpoint or service boundary] — make integration test pass

## Phase 4: Refactor

> **Rule:** All tests must remain passing after each refactor step.

- [ ] Refactor [component] for readability and maintainability
- [ ] Ensure code meets project conventions (naming, comments, documentation)
- [ ] Remove any duplication introduced during Green phase

## Phase 5: Integration & End-to-End Verification

- [ ] Run full test suite — all tests must be green
- [ ] Manually test the happy path scenario from the spec
- [ ] Manually test at least one error path scenario
- [ ] Invoke `security-auditor` subagent — resolve any CRITICAL or HIGH findings
- [ ] Invoke `dependency-auditor` subagent — resolve any vulnerable dependencies

## Phase 6: Documentation & Closeout

- [ ] Write `walkthrough.md` with summary of changes, test evidence, and diff
- [ ] Update `status` in `{{FEATURE_ID}}-spec` to `done`
- [ ] Update `status` in `{{FEATURE_ID}}-plan` to `done`
- [ ] Update `verified_by` in spec and plan with walkthrough `id`
- [ ] Create PR / commit with reference to spec `id`: `feat({{FEATURE_ID}}): ...`

